{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLWkGTeGE61CH7f3JUg9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I made the change: cloning a `Mesh`, `Line` or `Points` now gives the clone its own copy of the materials array. The materials themselves are still shared, as the issue asked. I haven't run any tests or tried it out.\n\nIn `copy()` in `src/objects/Mesh.js`, `src/objects/Line.js` and `src/objects/Points.js`, the material line is now:\n\n```js\nthis.material = Array.isArray( source.material ) ? source.material.slice() : source.material;\n```\n\n`clone()` calls `copy()`, so it picks this up. If `material` is a single material rather than an array, it is shared exactly as before.\n\nI left `Sprite.js` unchanged. A sprite only ever has one material, so it has no array to copy."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":316,"cache_read_input_tokens":18205,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":316},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6fedd534-3e02-4e41-bea8-f38625f13e98","uuid":"764e09a3-bf68-4895-ad8e-d1115ed09938","timestamp":"2026-11-23T20:45:45.221Z","request_id":"req_011ChLWkGNvYBqiJ6DLDoZDV"}
